Data

The name, company and place data comes from faux-person, which built it from
these sources. faux-person's own NOTICE, in its jar at META-INF/NOTICE, gives
the detail.

1. Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org), CC0 1.0: given and family names,
   their spellings in their own scripts, and company names, headquarters,
   countries and official websites.

2. GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org), licensed under the Creative Commons
   Attribution 4.0 License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/):
   the city and state for each ZIP code, and company headquarters resolved to
   a city. Changes: places were sampled per state, joined to postal codes, and
   reduced to name, state and one ZIP code.

3. US Census Bureau, TIGER/Line Shapefiles 2024, Address Features (ADDRFEAT):
   street names and ZIP codes. A work of the US Government, not subject to
   copyright in the United States.
